---
source: crates/pogo-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: help
---
Flash, reset, and capture in one step (the main agent command)

Usage: pogo run [OPTIONS] <IMAGE>

Arguments:
  <IMAGE>
          ELF (preferred) or raw .bin image

Options:
      --address <ADDR>
          Flash address for a raw .bin, e.g. 0x10000

      --chip <CHIP>
          Chip type [default: auto-detect]

      --flash-baud <BAUD>
          Baud rate used while flashing

      --bootloader <BIN>
          Custom bootloader image

      --partition-table <CSV|BIN>
          Custom partition table

      --no-verify
          Skip read-back verification

      --no-reset
          Stay in the bootloader after flashing

      --erase-all
          Erase the entire flash first (guarded; requires --confirm)

      --confirm <USB_SERIAL>
          USB serial of the device, confirming --erase-all

      --allow-bootloader-write
          Allow raw writes to the bootloader and partition table area

      --baud <N>
          Baud rate

      --until <REGEX>
          Stop with success when a line matches (repeatable)

      --fail-on <REGEX>
          Stop with TARGET_FAULT when a line matches (repeatable)

      --no-default-fail-patterns
          Don't use the built-in panic/abort/brownout patterns

      --settle <DURATION>
          Keep reading this long after an --until match to catch late crashes

      --max-lines <N>
          Maximum lines returned; extra lines are omitted from the middle
          
          [default: 500]

      --max-line-len <N>
          Maximum characters per line; longer lines are truncated
          
          [default: 1000]

      --parser <PARSER>
          Log line parser [default: the device's config, else auto]
          
          [possible values: auto, esp-idf, rust-log, raw]

      --elf <PATH>
          ELF used to symbolize backtraces

      --raw
          Keep ANSI escape codes

      --reconnect-timeout <DURATION>
          How long to wait for a vanished device to reappear (USB re-enumeration); 0 disables
          
          [default: 5s]

      --record <FILE>
          Save the raw byte stream with timestamps as JSONL

      --no-flash
          Skip flashing; reset and capture only

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
  -d, --device <SELECTOR>
          Target device: alias, USB serial, port, or "auto"

      --probe <SELECTOR>
          Probe device [default: "probe" alias, else auto]

  -f, --format <FORMAT>
          Output format [default: human]
          
          [env: POGO_FORMAT=]
          [possible values: human, json, jsonl]

      --config <PATH>
          Config file
          
          [env: POGO_CONFIG=]

      --timeout <DURATION>
          Overall deadline for this command, e.g. 500ms, 10s, 2m

      --wait-lock <DURATION>
          Wait for a busy device instead of failing

      --dry-run
          Describe what a mutating command would do; change nothing

  -v, --verbose...
          More logs on stderr (repeatable)

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only on stderr

      --no-color
          Disable colors

Locks the device once, flashes, resets into run mode, and captures from the first boot
byte. The exit code comes from the capture outcome unless flashing failed.

Examples:
  pogo run target/riscv32imc-unknown-none-elf/release/app --until READY -f json
  pogo run app.elf --no-flash --until READY --settle 2s

Exit codes: 0 matched, 3 device not found/ambiguous, 4 timeout, 6 device I/O,
7 target fault, 8 guardrail refused, 9 device busy

JSON data: { device, flash, capture } (see flash and serial capture)
